---
name: review-task
version: 3.8.0
description: lead phase-ending code review assignment for atm-bd-orchestration. task_id is a review bead the lead creates under the phase feature. Read-only; the lead files the findings as finding beads.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - phase
  - branch
  - commit
  - worktree_path
  - review_focus
  - review_questions
  - references
  - integration_branch
metadata:
  type: review-task
  tags:
    - stage:review
    - orchestration:beads
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: phase
      variable: phase
    state: review-start
    stage: review
    transition: start
---
<atm-review id="{{ task_id }}" phase="{{ phase }}">
  <description><![CDATA[Phase-ending code review and finding post-mortem on the integrated phase branch. Read-only analysis only; no code changes.]]></description>

  <branch><![CDATA[{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}]]></branch>
  <commit><![CDATA[{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}]]></commit>
  <worktree><![CDATA[{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}]]></worktree>

  <review-focus><![CDATA[
{{ review_focus | string | cdata_escape }}
  ]]></review-focus>

  <review-questions><![CDATA[
{{ review_questions | string | cdata_escape }}
  ]]></review-questions>

  <references><![CDATA[
{{ references | string | cdata_escape }}
  ]]></references>

  <output-format><![CDATA[
    Structured findings report, sections in order:
    1. SUMMARY — one-paragraph verdict
    2. FINDINGS — numbered list, each with severity (blocking, important, minor), location, finding, recommendation
    3. EXTRACTION-READINESS — score 1-5 per relevant module with rationale
    4. RECOMMENDED-NEXT-SPRINTS — concrete follow-up work
    5. INTEGRATION POST-MORTEM — follow .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/references/post-mortem.md: all finding ids and dispositions, evidence at the assigned integration SHA, inventory totals, integration_review_passed or integration_review_failed, useful systemic follow-ups (or none).
  ]]></output-format>

  <workflow>
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Check readiness, claim the bead, then start the task. If not ready, do not claim or start; refuse as in step d1 (`bead_state` `open`), `reason_md` naming the bead, its blockers, which bead or agent has to move, and, for a blocker not yet its dependency, the edge `bd dep add {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --blocked-by <blocker>`; never wait.]]></step>
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[Require branch `{{ integration_branch | string | cdata_escape }}` (the phase root's `metadata.integration_branch`); a stack-tip review cannot substitute for integration verification. Verify `{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}` is on `{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}` with `HEAD` exactly `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}`; reject a mismatched or moving checkout. Read relevant source and docs at that commit with `git show {{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}:<path>`. Phase plan: `bd show <phase feature>` and its children (`bd list --parent <phase feature> --all -n 0`).]]></step>
    <step id="b1"><![CDATA[Read .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/references/post-mortem.md; reconcile every phase finding, including closed and nested ones, at the assigned commit. Run the JEV workflow in references/post-mortem-context-preparation.md, then investigate every unsure/flagged result. Populate `integration_review`, `post_mortem_md`, and `post_mortem_jev` (status, run_ids, jsonl_path, integration_sha, reason) in the completion variables. JEV unavailability or unchecked findings leave integration review pending: do not close the bead; refuse as in step d1 with `REVIEW_PENDING_JEV` instead of `REVIEW_CANNOT_RUN`, putting every code finding and `post_mortem_jev` (status `unavailable`, with run IDs so far) in the refusal's `notes_md` for the task assigner to file; announce a persistent Jev outage as a serious failure (`.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/SKILL.md`, Lead Role). Missing or unverified resolutions prevent an integration PASS.]]></step>
    <step id="c"><![CDATA[Do not make any code changes and do not write to any bead except claiming, closing or returning this review bead; the task assigner files each finding as a finding bead from your report.]]></step>
    <step id="d"><![CDATA[Re-verify every cited file:line at `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}`, never a newer branch tip or moving worktree state; stale or missing evidence is a finding, not a guess. Before closing, run `python3 .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/check-review-completion.py <scratch>/review-complete-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`; require exit 0. It checks counts, verdict and the pinned SHA, not source evidence truth. Then close bead and task together, `bd close` first; close the task only if `bd close` succeeded: `bd close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --reason "review complete: <verdict>"` and `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} completed --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/review-complete.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/review-complete-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`, vars built from that template's `required_variables` (`task_id`, `phase` and `commit` unchanged) and written outside the repository. Only this close frees your queue.]]></step>
    <step id="d1"><![CDATA[If the review cannot run, reuse the existing workflow class bead with the same failure signature: append the task id, head, command and failure evidence, and cite the class id in the refusal. If no class matches, report the signature to the task assigner for classification and cite that message instead; do not create a per-task shadow or delay the refusal. Return the bead with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "REVIEW_CANNOT_RUN; workflow class or escalation <reference>: <reason>"` and close the task with `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} refused --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/task-refused.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/refused-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`. A blocker is not a failure: when a prerequisite reopens or the work needs an unlanded fix, stop, return the bead with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "BLOCKED: <blocker>: <why>"` and close the task `refused` as above (`bead_state` `open`), `reason_md` naming the blocker and the edge `bd dep add {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --blocked-by <blocker>`; never stay active waiting.]]></step>
  </workflow>
</atm-review>
